atd 0.1
part of wardley/map

// The Online Wardley Maps text format (definitions/diagrams/wardley-map.dis, wardley-map.md): an `.owm` or `.wm` file
// body, registered by an .adp file whose origin is wardley/map. No FBL family reads it as the tool does (gaps 1 to 6:
// a pipeline whose brace is on the line below, decorators in any order, an annotation's positions, the identity file
// beside the body), so it is read and written by the capability reader.onlineWardleyMaps, named for the format, which
// delivers the model's own types. A new map is `title {base}` and a line ending.

binding owm family capability reader.onlineWardleyMaps {
  label "Online Wardley Maps"
  claims {
    extensions: [".owm", ".wm"]
    origins: ["wardley/map"]
  }
  template {
    text: """title {base}
"""
  }
}
